ement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-05\nValid as Of: 2023-10-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4110 ---\nComponent: UI5 Flexibility for Key Users\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Publishing UI Changes\nDescription: You can publish UI changes and then transport them to another subaccount using the SAP Content Agent service.  See Publishing UI Changes.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-05\nValid as Of: 2023-10-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 3691 ---\nComponent: Cloud Portal Service\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: End Of Maintenance for SAP Cloud Portal service, version 1.0 (Neo Environment)\nDescription: SAP Cloud Portal service, version 1.0 on the Neo Environment will reach the status End-of-Maintenance on 31st December 2023.  This version of SAP Cloud Portal service will be deprecated on 25th January 2024, and from that point on, access to this service won’t be possible.  SAP Cloud Portal service, version 2.0 on the Neo Environment, released in December 2015, is not affected by this change.    Note  To verify which version you’re using, please note the differences in the site URL:     Scenario  Version 1.0  Version 2.0        Design time  URL ends with /portal/index.html  URL contains adminspace      Runtime  URL contains /portal/cloud-portal/index.html  URL contains dispatcher      \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-31\nValid as Of: 2023-12-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3692 ---\nComponent: SAP Conversational AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Tenant Header Configuration Endpoint\nDescription: As of June 2023, /auth/v1/update_tenant_security_header_toggle has been deprectaed. For more information, see API documentation.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-07-05\nValid as Of: 2023-12-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3693 ---\nComponent: SAP Conversational AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Tenant Security Headers\nDescription: As of June 2023, you must configure tenant security headers for your enterprise tenant. You cannot set security header toggle for your enterprise tenant to false using the Tenant Header Configuration endpoint. See Configure Tenant Security Headers.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-07-05\nValid as Of: 2023-12-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3694 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Aligned Tile Behavior\nDescription: Until now, certain application tiles such as Dynamic tiles and tiles with custom images, behaved differently when accessed from a workpage rather than through the Applications page. This behavior has been aligned and now all application tiles behave the same no matter where they are accessed from.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-21\nValid as Of: 2023-12-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3695 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Integration with Central Notification\nDescription: Site administrators can choose whether to use the default notification mechanism available in their site, or to enable the integration with central notification, and show notifications from multiple notification providers. As part of this change, part of the notifications will be migrated to the Task Center.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-21\nValid as Of: 2023-12-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3696 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Menu Workpage Widgets Can Reference Contents From Workspaces\nDescription: Widgets in workpages ,which are part of the site menu, can reference content from any public or private workspace. Supported widgets are Multimedia, Image, Poll, Slide Show, and Rotating Banner widgets.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-21\nValid as Of: 2023-12-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3697 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Updated Collaboration Level for Non-Members on Public Workspaces\nDescription: While the collaboration levels of workspace members remain Full, Limited, and Read-Only, the collaboration level for non-members on public workspaces now includes two options: Same as members, and None.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-21\nValid as Of: 2023-12-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3698 ---\nComponent: SAP Start\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP Task Center integration is optional\nDescription: In an existing subscription setup, integration with SAP Task Center is optional. However, once the setup is complete, it is no longer possible to add SAP Task Center, and the To-Dos section will not be displayed.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-28\nValid as Of: 2023-12-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3699 ---\nComponent: SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud for Credit Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New App: Display Status Log for Credit Reports (F7891)\nDescription: Use this app to see the status log of imported credit reports and monitoring notifications for your business partners. If errors occurred during the import, the app provides more details.  More information:   Display Status Log for Credit Reports  Displaying Logs for External Credit Information\nAction: Info only\n", "3699 ---\nComponent: SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud for Credit Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New App: Display Status Log for Credit Reports (F7891)\nDescription: Use this app to see the status log of imported credit reports and monitoring notifications for your business partners. If errors occurred during the import, the app provides more details.  More information:   Display Status Log for Credit Reports  Displaying Logs for External Credit Information\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-27\nValid as Of: 2023-12-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3700 ---\nComponent: Peppol Exchange\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Enhancements to the service for Germany\nDescription: The following enhancements are only relevant for Germany and have already been updated in the test environment:      Updated XRechnung standard to version 3.0.1.      Updated schematron file for XRechnung to version 2.0.1. This version is compatible with XRechnung 3.0.1.      This change will be active in the production environment on the next deployment planned to take place on December 30, 2023.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2023-12-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 241 ---\nComponent: Responsibility Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Migrate Personal Data Management to Data Privacy Integration NextGen\nDescription: Data Privacy Integration NextGen (DPI NextGen) service is the natural unified successor of Personal Data Manager (Information Reporting of personal data), Data Retention Manager (Blocking and Deletion of personal data), Consent Repository services and the existing DPI Kernel Service. The service offers a unified data privacy experience by bringing all DPP capabilities into one single service that is capable of being hosted on both CF and Kyma runtimes. For more information, see Data Privacy Integration NextGen.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-18\nValid as Of: 2025-08-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 242 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Core\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: New models are supported, including GPT 5, GPT 5 Mini, and GPT 5 Nano.For more information, see SAP Note 3437766 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-18\nValid as Of: 2025-08-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 243 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: New models are supported, including GPT 5, GPT 5 Mini, and GPT 5 Nano.For more information, see SAP Note 3437766 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-18\nValid as Of: 2025-08-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 244 ---\nComponent: SAP Build\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Create Full-Stack ABAP Projects\nDescription: The following options are available:     You can now create full-stack ABAP projects using the ABAP development tools. This allows you to build complete applications based on the ABAP Cloud development model. For more information, see Full-Stack ABAP Project Creation Using Development Tools.      You can now create full-stack ABAP projects using the Business Application Studio. This allows you to develop remote applications for modeling business objects using the ABAP Cloud development model. For more information, see Full-Stack ABAP Project Creation Using SAP Business Application Studio. For more information, see Full-Stack ABAP Project Creation Using SAP Business Application Studio.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-19\nValid as Of: 2025-08-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 245 ---\nComponent: SAP Business Application Studio\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Development Experience\nDescription: You can now develop a full-stack ABAP application in SAP Business Application Studio by creating a Full-Stack ABAP Cloud project, model the application with the CDS Graphical Modeler, generate ABAP CDS artifacts, and develop a user interface. See Develop a Full-Stack ABAP Application in SAP Business Application Studio.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-18\nValid as Of: 2025-08-18\nVersion: T2507b\n\n--- Record 246 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Manage Security Audit Log (F6996A) (Deprecated)\nDescription: The Manage Security Audit Log app (App ID: F6996) is now deprecated and will be removed from the SAP Fiori launchpad in an upcoming release.  This app has been replaced by its successor, Manage Security Audit Log (App ID: F6996A), which offers improved functionality and aligns with the latest SAP Fiori design standards.  See Manage Security Audit Log (Deprecated).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 247 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Enhanced Intelligent Scenarios in Sales for SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition\nDescription: You can activate the deployment of the intelligent scenarios to consume the inference in your business application, using the following:     2023: SD_INT_AI_GEMINI, SD_INT_AI_GPT. When more than one scenario is active, the system prioritizes the SD_INT_AI_GPT scenario for consumption.    For more information, see Activate and Deactivate and Perform Sales Order Field Changes and Resolve Fulfillment Issues.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-11\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 248 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: ADT Debugger Comparison Tool for Internal Tables\nDescription: With the table comparison tool within the ADT debugger, you can now compare internal tables in ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse.  See Comparing Internal Tables.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: nan\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 249 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\n", " Internal Tables\nDescription: With the table comparison tool within the ADT debugger, you can now compare internal tables in ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse.  See Comparing Internal Tables.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: nan\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 249 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Creation of Behavior Definition for CDS Table Entities\nDescription: You can now create behavior definitions for CDS table entities. CDS table entities describe physical database tables in the SAP HANA database that is connected to the current AS ABAP.  See Table Entities and Creating Data Definitions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: nan\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 250 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Display of Copyright Statement for ABAP Development Objects in Properties View\nDescription: You can now see the copyright statement for ABAP development objects in the Properties view.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: nan\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n", "--- Record 221 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Document Grounding Capability - Get Pipeline Status\nDescription: The available statuses for pipelines, executions, and documents have been updated.  See Get Pipeline Status.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-10\nValid as Of: 2025-08-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 222 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Document Grounding Capability - Search Pipelines\nDescription: You can now send a POST request to the endpoint <url>/pipeline/api/v1/pipeline/search to see a list of document grounding pipelines that match the metadata specified in the request body.  See Search Pipelines.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-10\nValid as Of: 2025-08-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 223 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Document Grounding Capability - Set Up Content Ingestion\nDescription: SharePoint can now have a folder depth of 5: In other words, it supports up to 5 levels in the folder hierarchy.  When setting up a pipeline, you can now schedule it to be automatically triggered at a frequency of your choice. You do so using cronExpression.  See Set Up Content Ingestion.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-10\nValid as Of: 2025-08-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 224 ---\nComponent: Multitarget Applications for Cloud Foundry\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: General support for CF app features\nDescription: You can manage whether optional capabilities are enabled for a given Cloud Foundry application with the app-features module-specific parameter. It accepts a map as a value, where all elements in the map are passed directly to the CF API. This mechanism ensures that all future app features will be automatically supported through MTA deployment.  The parameter is especially useful when many services are bound to an application, and all credentials inside the VCAP_SERVICES environment variable exceed the maximum size of 130 KB (see Cloud Foundry environment variables). In this case, the application cannot be staged successfully. To solve that issue, you can switch to the \"file-based VCAP services\" method by enabling the respective app feature, and adapt your application coding accordingly to use a file instead of the VCAP_SERVICES environment variable. See Delivering service credentials to an app.  For more information about the parameter, see Module-Specific Parameters.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-21\nValid as Of: 2025-08-21\nVersion: 2508a\n\n--- Record 225 ---\nComponent: SAP Authorization and Trust Management service,SAP BTP Connectivity,SAP Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Principal propagation from SAP BTP to an On-Premise Cloud Connector with a Token From a Corporate Identity Provider\nDescription: You have or develop SAP BTP applications which interact with on-premise applications for which you don't want to accept tokens from SAP BTP identity and access management services, namely SAP Cloud Identity Services and SAP Authorization and Trust Management service. You can configure SAP BTP applications to include a token from the corporate identity provider you trust.  For more information, see Principal Propagation from BTP Applications to On-Premise Systems Using Corporate IdP Tokens.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-21\nValid as Of: 2025-08-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 226 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 51.0.0\nDescription: Cloud Foundry has been updated from 50.4.0 to 51.0.0.    https://github.com/cloudfoundry/c